{title: Jesus, Touch Me (FJ_110_en)}
{song_number: 110}
{language: en}
{tempo: 126}
{artist: Albert Frey}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D]If I touch the hem of your garment [Bm7]for a single moment,
[Dmaj7]I will feel the power going out from you [Asus4]deep within me. [A]
[D]Just one glance from your eyes, just one [Bm7]word from your mouth,
[Dmaj7]and the streams of healing flow; my [Asus4]soul will be made whole. [A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Jesus, touch me. Come and meet me, open the [Em7]door for me.
Take me by the hand and [G]lead me into your [Bm7]presence. [A]
[D]Jesus, I sense you; I reach out to you and [Em7]touch you.
And my heart burns anew, only for [G]you, here in your [Bm7]presence. [A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D]Just one piece of the bread of life, one [Bm7]drop from the cup,
[Dmaj7]and I am joined with you, and [Asus4]my hunger is satisfied. [A]
[D]Just one sip from the river of life, from the [Bm7]water you give,
[Dmaj7]and the streams begin to flow from the [Asus4]spring deep within me. [A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Jesus, touch me. Come and meet me, open the [Em7]door for me.
Take me by the hand and [G]lead me into your [Bm7]presence. [A]
[D]Jesus, I sense you; I reach out to you and [Em7]touch you.
And my heart burns anew, only for [G]you, here in your [Bm7]presence. [A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[D/F#]Lord, I am not worthy; [G]I am often far from [A]you.
[D/F#]Yet in your love [G]you come to me [A]too.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Jesus, touch me. Come and meet me, open the [Em7]door for me.
Take me by the hand and [G]lead me into your [Bm7]presence. [A]
[D]Jesus, I sense you; I reach out to you and [Em7]touch you.
And my heart burns anew, only for [G]you, here in your [Bm7]presence. [A]
{end_of_chorus}
